### 1. The Auto-Refresh Implementation (`handleNext`)

To implement the auto-refresh, we will catch the `409 Conflict` error when User B tries to lock a VID that User A just took. When this happens, we will show the error, clear their selection, and instantly re-fetch the list from the database. Because the database query automatically filters out locked/used VIDs, the taken VID will instantly vanish from their screen.

Here is the exact updated `handleNext` function to replace your current one:

```javascript
  const handleNext = async () => {
    if (activeStep === 0) {
      if (!selectedVoucher) {
        showSnackBar("Please select a voucher from the list first.", "warning");
        return;
      }

      // --- ACQUIRE THE PESSIMISTIC LOCK ---
      const vidToLock = selectedVoucher.vid || selectedVoucher.VID;
      setIsPageLoading(true);
      
      try {
        await callApi(`/JS/voucher/lock/${vidToLock}`, null, "POST");
        lockedVidRef.current = vidToLock; // Store the successfully locked VID
        setActiveStep((prevStep) => prevStep + 1); // Proceed to Entry Method
      } catch (error) {
        // 1. Show the "Already in Use" message
        const errMsg = error?.response?.data?.message || "This VID is already in use by another user.";
        showSnackBar(errMsg, "warning");
        
        // 2. Clear the current selection so it doesn't stay highlighted
        setSelectedVoucher(null);
        
        // 3. Auto-Refresh the Grid
        try {
          let actualRoleId = currentRoleId;
          if (!actualRoleId) {
             const auth = sessionStorage.getItem("persist:auth") || localStorage.getItem("persist:auth");
             if (auth) {
               const user = JSON.parse(JSON.parse(auth).user);
               actualRoleId = user?.roleId || user?.role || user?.ROLE_ID;
             }
          }
          
          if (actualRoleId) {
            const vouchersResponse = await callApi(`/JS/voucher/active?roleId=${actualRoleId}`, null, "GET");
            const fetchedVouchers = vouchersResponse?.data || vouchersResponse || [];
            setVoucherList(Array.isArray(fetchedVouchers) ? fetchedVouchers : []);
          }
        } catch (refreshErr) {
          console.error("Failed to auto-refresh voucher list", refreshErr);
        }
      } finally {
        setIsPageLoading(false);
      }
    } else {
      // Normal progression for other steps
      setActiveStep((prevStep) => prevStep + 1);
    }
  };

```

### 2. The Combined Tab-Close Logic

Since you already have a `beforeunload` event listener checking if the user abandons Step 3, we need to combine the lock release into that existing block.

